# A first-level heading inside the writing

This intentionally repeats the first heading level to make its body styling easy to compare with the entry title.

## A second-level heading

This is the normal section heading used throughout an entry.

### A third-level heading

A smaller section within the same line of thought.

#### A fourth-level heading

A brief aside within that section.

##### A fifth-level heading

A finer division, included here for completeness.

###### A sixth-level heading

The smallest available heading level. The final paragraph brings us back to ordinary reading, with **bold**, *italic*, ~~strikethrough~~, `inline code`, and a [return to all entries](/).

